The rule for `_grounding_kernel` says the verdict is one of "GROUNDED, SPAN_MISSING, SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT or VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN" and that the value-in-span check is on. Changing the value from "cat" to "dog" while keeping the same span and document should move the verdict from GROUNDED to VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN, so the rule as written says the check's answer ought to move.